{"id":9054031,"docketId":66320277,"caseName":"Brogdon v. Louisiana","caseNameFull":"Brogdon v. Louisiana Fairchild v. Arkansas Hall v. Wainwright, Secretary, Florida Department of Corrections Singleton v. South Carolina Stano v. Florida Washington v. Virginia Dutton v. Oklahoma Carriger v. Arizona","slug":"brogdon-v-louisiana","docketNumber":"No. 84-6033; No. 84-6284; No. 84-6326; No. 84-6408; No. 84-6413; No. 84-6486; No. 84-6490; No. 84-65","dateFiled":"1985-05-13","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1985,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":220,"judges":"Brennan, Marshall","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":9047533,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1915,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<p id=\"Artu\">Sup. Ct. La.;</p>\n<p id=\"A-WH\">Sup. Ct. Ark.;</p>\n<p id=\"AN2L\">C. A. 11th Cir.;</p>\n<p id=\"AVJv\">Sup. Ct. S. C.;</p>\n<p id=\"AbRI\">Sup. Ct. Fla.;</p>\n<p id=\"AbBq\">Sup. Ct. Va.;</p>\n<p id=\"Ake\">Ct. Crim. App. Okla.; and</p>\n<p id=\"Av7\">Sup. Ct. Ariz. Cer-tiorari denied. Reported below: No. 84-6033, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1129583\"><a href=\"/opinion/1129583/state-v-brogdon/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Brogdon\">457 So. 2d 616</a></span>; No. 84-6284, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1530912\"><a href=\"/opinion/1530912/fairchild-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Fairchild v. State\">284 Ark. 289</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1530912\"><a href=\"/opinion/1530912/fairchild-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Fairchild v. State\">681 S. W. 2d 380</a></span>; No. 84-6326, <span class=\"citation multiple-matches\"><a href=\"/c/F.%202d/733/766/\">733 F. 2d 766</a></span>; No. 84-6408, 284 S. C. 388, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1250643\"><a href=\"/opinion/1250643/state-v-singleton/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Singleton\">326 S. E. 2d 153</a></span>; No. 84-6413, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1938291\"><a href=\"/opinion/1938291/stano-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Stano v. State\">460 So. 2d 890</a></span>; No. 84-6486, <span class=\"citation multiple-matches\"><a href=\"/c/Va./228/535/\">228 Va. 535</a></span>, <span class=\"citation multiple-matches\"><a href=\"/c/S.%20E.%202d/323/577/\">323 S. E. 2d 577</a></span>; No. 84-6526, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9547568\"><a href=\"/opinion/1173286/state-v-carriger/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Carriger\">143 Ariz. 142</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9547568\"><a href=\"/opinion/1173286/state-v-carriger/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Carriger\">692 P. 2d 991</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9047534,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":598,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b1045-13\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"Av0\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b1045-14\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}